dit/083: ggml-opencl's Adreno xmem attention keeps its scores in fp32. It summed Q.K in fp16 and stored the scores,
the row max and 1/sum in fp16: at logits in the hundreds an fp16 score is +-0.5 and the softmax goes wrong. Z-Image's
attention is that sharp and rendered as stripes (Klein's is not). nm-fa-check (dit/082), 1280 tokens, 30 heads, q and k
std 30: 10% error with fp16 scores, 2e-5 on the generic path. Now: fp32 accumulators in the QK gemm, fp32 score and
probability buffers and images, fp32 softmax stats; the PV gemm still reads the probabilities as half (they are in
[0, 1]). Applies after 080 and 081.

